{
  "cells": [
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "---\n",
        "title: \"Population-Level Correlation Analysis\"\n",
        "format: html\n",
        "---\n",
        "\n",
        "## What This Code Does\n",
        "\n",
        "This demo runs a full simulation and extracts population-level time series data (averages across all agents per step). It computes a Pearson correlation matrix on population means: avg PSS-10, resilience, affect, stress, resources, social support rate, and coping success rate.\n",
        "\n",
        "Population-level correlations reveal emergent macro-patterns that arise from individual agent interactions — distinct from agent-level correlations in the previous demo.\n",
        "\n",
        "## Setup"
      ],
      "id": "e980a986"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "#| label: setup\n",
        "import os\n",
        "import sys\n",
        "import pathlib\n",
        "import numpy as np\n",
        "import pandas as pd\n",
        "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
        "import seaborn as sns\n",
        "\n",
        "demos_dir = pathlib.Path(os.getcwd())\n",
        "project_root = demos_dir.parents[2]\n",
        "sys.path.insert(0, str(project_root))\n",
        "\n",
        "from src.python.model import StressModel"
      ],
      "id": "setup",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## Simulation"
      ],
      "id": "0d8f4d5a"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "#| label: simulate\n",
        "days, agents, seed = 100, 30, 42\n",
        "print(f\"Running simulation with {agents} agents for {days} days (seed={seed})...\")\n",
        "model = StressModel(N=agents, max_days=days, seed=seed)\n",
        "while model.running:\n",
        "    model.step()\n",
        "\n",
        "model_data = model.get_time_series_data()\n",
        "print(f\"Simulation done. Data shape: {model_data.shape}\")"
      ],
      "id": "simulate",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## Correlation Matrix"
      ],
      "id": "7619b649"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "#| label: corr\n",
        "vars_of_interest = [\"avg_pss10\", \"avg_resilience\", \"avg_affect\", \"avg_stress\", \"avg_resources\", \"social_support_rate\", \"coping_success_rate\"]\n",
        "available = [v for v in vars_of_interest if v in model_data.columns]\n",
        "print(f\"Analyzing: {available}\")\n",
        "\n",
        "corr = model_data[available].corr()\n",
        "print(corr.to_string(float_format=\"%.4f\"))"
      ],
      "id": "corr",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## Interpretation"
      ],
      "id": "ae7a3f52"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "#| label: interpret\n",
        "for i, v1 in enumerate(available):\n",
        "    for j, v2 in enumerate(available):\n",
        "        if i < j:\n",
        "            r = corr.loc[v1, v2]\n",
        "            strength = \"Strong\" if abs(r) > 0.7 else \"Moderate\" if abs(r) > 0.3 else \"Weak\"\n",
        "            direction = \"positive\" if r > 0 else \"negative\"\n",
        "            print(f\"{v1} ↔ {v2}: {strength} {direction} (r={r:.4f})\")"
      ],
      "id": "interpret",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## Why This Matters for the Simulation\n",
        "\n",
        "Population-level correlations capture emergent dynamics that agent-level analysis may miss. For example, a strong correlation between avg_stress and coping_success_rate may indicate that the population adapts to stress over time — or that high stress overwhelms coping capacity. These patterns validate the model's aggregate behaviour against theoretical expectations."
      ],
      "id": "ccb47cf7"
    }
  ],
